  "answer": "According to web sources retrieved on October 27, 2026:\n\n* **Architect:** The Sydney Opera House was designed by Danish architect Jørn Utzon, who won an international design competition for the project announced in 1957 [W1], [W3]. Following Utzon's departure from the project in 1966, construction was completed by an Australian architectural team headed by Peter Hall [W1], [W2].\n* **Opening Date:** The building was formally opened by Queen Elizabeth II on October 20, 1973 [W1]."
